## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to coordinate API server webhook rollout, CA rotation, and observability without service disruption. Highlights risk detection and rollback discipline.

## Key Concepts

- MutatingWebhookConfiguration
- CA bundle rotation and webhooks
- RollingUpdate strategy
- Canary deployment patterns
- cluster observability and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code using Kubernetes client (Node.js)
const k8s = require('@kubernetes/client-node');
const kc = new k8s.KubeConfig();
kc.loadFromDefault();
const k8sApi = kc.makeApiClient(k8s.AdmissionregistrationV1Api);
await k8sApi.patchMutatingWebhookConfiguration('obs-sidecar', {
  // patch body
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor TLS handshake failures and distinguish node-specific issues from cluster-wide problems?
- What are safe rollback criteria and automatic rollback triggers for webhook upgrades?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical disaster recovery skills for an etcd-backed control plane, including backup verification, restore sequencing, API server restart order, and RBAC/certs rotation under downtime pressure.

## Key Concepts

- etcd backup/restore and snapshot integrity
- API server restart order and kubeadm reconfiguration
- RBAC, cert rotation, and smoke tests

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple script skeleton for backup verification
const {execSync} = require('child_process');
try {
  console.log(execSync('etcdctl snapshot status /backups/etcd-snapshot.db').toString());
} catch (e) {
  console.error('Backup check failed', e);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle multi-tenant workloads during restore?
- What metrics indicate a healthy restoration?
